   "id": "yevamot.47b.13",
   "daf": "47b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "נִתְרַפֵּא — מַטְבִּילִין אוֹתוֹ מִיָּד. נִתְרַפֵּא — אִין, לֹא נִתְרַפֵּא — לָא. מַאי טַעְמָא? מִשּׁוּם דְּמַיָּא מַרְזוּ מַכָּה.",
   "en": "The baraita continues: When «he is healed» from the circumcision, «they immerse him immediately.» The Gemara infers from the precise formulation of the baraita that when «he has healed,» then «yes,» he is immersed, but as long as «he has not healed,» then «no,» he is not. «What is the reason» for this? It is «because water agitates a wound.»"
  }
 ],
